ainst a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not triggered and the request that this case be escalated is rejected on that ground.\n\nNo other exculpatory route is open: POL-RD-04 (no chat messages; EV-CHAT-02840 has 0), POL-RD-05 (no amended endpoints; amended_optimal_distance_km is null), POL-RD-12 (vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL), POL-RD-11 (fare_model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE).\n\nThe remedy (POL-RD-02). fare_model is METERED. charged_total = 51.38 (EV-FARE-02840). The surge multiplier 1.4 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and nowhere else. Recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 20.0 + 0.28 x 26.0) x 1.4) + 0.80 platform fee = (26.08 x 1.4) + 0.80 = 36.512 + 0.80 = 37.312. Refund = 51.38 - 37.312 = 14.068, rounded UP to SGD 14.10. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and is 27.38% of charged_total, short of the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 14.10. The SGD 25.00 the rider contests is not supported by the policy's arithmetic.\n\nNothing is added or netted (POL-RD-09). No ERP gantries, zero tolls, no airport surcharge (the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport), so there is no pass-through or billing-integrity correction and no POL-RD-09(4) referral. No driver compensation under POL-RD-04: distance_charged_km (29.0) equals the trace distance, so there are no unbilled kilometres.\n\nConfidence is 0.90, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-GPS-02840, EV-TRIP-02840, EV-FARE-02840). The refund of SGD 14.10 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so the amount is issued but held for human release rather than executed automatically; that holding is procedural and does not change the ruling. This ruling is provisional and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
